inian counterparts  cannot dedicate 100  of time to that work  mrs vasilenko on the political front  you've recently been very critical of  the un secretary general antonio  gutierrez because he went to moscow a  few days ago before going to kiev what  did he bring back from russia anything  that your government thought was worth  listening to  he brought back a missile attack on the  building in kiev  which was destroyed and several people  died from from that missile attack and  a 10 or so were  injured and taken to hospital with heavy  wounds  apart from that  not much  has resulted  not really his fault though  not not really his fault no but uh you  know uh the point is that uh i think the  he uh and this is the point that i tried  to make many many times is that the u.n  needs reform  the u.n as a system has failed has  failed big time to prevent wars in the  past and to prevent this war of russia's  aggression which has been going on for  eight years now russia staying on the  security council having veto power is  absolute nonsense i mean russia is  responsible for the insecurity in the  world and the instability in the world  today and they are there making security  decisions  uh we have as ukrainians time and time  again raise the issue about the reform  of the of the un system we were not hurt  um  then when we have the secretary general  first going to moscow and then coming to  q  that also doesn't make sense why go and  do pay the respects and the jews to the  aggressive us come come to ukraine see  what russia has done and then go to  putin with the demands not the other way  around this was the point i was trying  to make but okay to be fair to be fair  uh after the secretary general's visit  the evacuation of the people from other  style and other styles still works in uh  in mario paul has started  uh and has had many successes so i'm  grateful for that i would love to  believe that it's because there was  these negotiations with the un secretary 